    "label_en": "Anuak (Anywaa) communities (as recorded by Seligman, 1932)",
    "label_ar": "مجتمعات الأنواك (كما سجّلها سليغمان، 1932) [يحتاج تحقق]",
    "label_note": "As recorded by Seligman, 1932. A 1910s–30s ethnographic record, not a present-day homeland or a claim about current territory.",
    "page_cites": [
     "p.105",
     "p.108"
    ],
    "basis": "Seligman & Seligman 1932, p.105, p.108: limits stated in the text only. Quote: p.105: 'The Anuak ... of the Sobat river, extending along the Baro and Akobo rivers into Abyssinia.' p.108: 'At the present day the Anuak inhabit the banks of the Baro, Gila, and Akobo rivers, extending into Abyssinia, with villages on the Sobat near Nasser and at Ajungmir near the mouth of the Pibor river ... formerly they lived lower down the Sobat whence they were driven eastwards by the Jekan Nuer.'",
    "method": "Text-limit redraw. Only the limits stated on p.105, p.108 are used; no coordinate is invented. Named places from Wikidata P625. Rivers: Natural Earth 10m rivers/lake centrelines (White Nile, Bahr el Jebel, Sobat, Akobo); Baro: OpenStreetMap ways (ODbL). Projection for distances: local equirectangular at 9°N. Bank bands are 10 km each side or on the stated bank (EDITORIAL width; the pages give banks, not widths).",
    "edges": {
     "Baro banks, 10 km band": "STATED river (pp.105, 108); width EDITORIAL",
     "Akobo banks, 10 km band": "STATED river (pp.105, 108); width EDITORIAL",
